00:09:14.119 --> 00:09:16.288
So we'll start with 1970,

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:19.791
and there were fewer, like,
solos and stuff like that.

00:09:19.791 --> 00:09:21.093
It was a little more rh--

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:22.895
They had more, like, rhythm
to it and percussion.

00:09:22.895 --> 00:09:24.763
So, like, something like
Velvet Underground

00:09:24.763 --> 00:09:29.201
was kind of like...

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:32.404
♪ Going down the boulevard
with the flower ♪

00:09:32.404 --> 00:09:34.072
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:34.072 --> 00:09:36.042
That kind of thing, right?

00:09:36.042 --> 00:09:38.944
[ Laughter ]

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:40.379
-Boulevard.

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:43.749
-So then like --
So then like mid-'70s,

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:47.619
there was stuff like the Ramones
and the stuff at CBGB's,

00:09:47.619 --> 00:09:52.558
very driving like...

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:55.060
♪ I just want to watch TV ♪

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:57.963
♪ My baby's giving me
a lobotomy ♪

00:09:57.963 --> 00:10:02.201
[ Both singing gibberish ]

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.935
That kind of thing.
-Yeah.

00:10:03.935 --> 00:10:07.073
-But then in --

00:10:07.073 --> 00:10:09.275
-Going down the boulevard
with a flower.

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:11.476
[ Laughter ]

00:10:11.476 --> 00:10:15.915
-And then, in England, like
1977, same kind of thing,

00:10:15.915 --> 00:10:21.053
but, like, a little more angular
and sort of like...

00:10:21.053 --> 00:10:23.555
♪ Don't go to the ambulance ♪

00:10:23.555 --> 00:10:27.860
♪ Don't go to the ambulance,
don't go to the ambulance ♪

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.828
♪ -Don't run on ♪
Yeah, love that.

00:10:29.828 --> 00:10:31.697
-Yeah, that kind of thing.
-Yeah.

00:10:31.697 --> 00:10:33.965
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:10:33.965 --> 00:10:38.070
Then like 1980, like post-punk,

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.239
they sort of, like, didn't do
chords that much.

00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:44.377
It was a little bit more like...

00:10:44.377 --> 00:10:46.912
♪ I am a neon light ♪

00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:51.416
[ Laughter ]

00:10:51.416 --> 00:10:53.352
-Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:53.352 --> 00:10:56.722
♪ I am a neon light ♪

00:10:56.722 --> 00:10:59.158
♪ I am the neon light ♪

00:10:59.158 --> 00:11:00.993
Yeah, that's great. Love that.

00:11:00.993 --> 00:11:03.295
-Then early '80s, there was like

00:11:03.295 --> 00:11:05.764
a sort of like country music
feel to, like, punk.

00:11:05.764 --> 00:11:08.600
It was kind of like...

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:15.774
[ Singing indistinctly ]

00:11:15.774 --> 00:11:17.543
Yeah, that kind of thing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:17.543 --> 00:11:23.549
And then there was like
a sort of mid-'80s, late '80s,

00:11:23.549 --> 00:11:26.752
like Sonic Youth would do this
thing where, like, the chords

00:11:26.752 --> 00:11:28.153
would be a little discordant.

00:11:28.153 --> 00:11:35.226
So it'd be like...

00:11:35.226 --> 00:11:38.163
♪ Candlelight ♪

00:11:38.163 --> 00:11:40.633
♪ On a booth ♪

00:11:40.633 --> 00:11:42.000
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.737
[ Cheers and applause ]
Wow. That's exactly right. Yeah.

00:11:44.737 --> 00:11:46.071
I remember that.

00:11:46.071 --> 00:11:48.740
-And then, do you remember
the early '90s,

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.308
like a little ska thing
happening?

00:11:50.308 --> 00:11:53.179
And very playful,
kind of like...

00:11:53.179 --> 00:11:54.479
-Yep.

00:11:54.479 --> 00:11:56.915
♪ -Your mom and dad were
the best you ever had ♪

00:11:56.915 --> 00:12:00.786
[ Both singing gibberish ]

00:12:00.786 --> 00:12:02.054
-Yeah, yeah.

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:04.557
-That kind of thing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:04.557 --> 00:12:08.760
And then Seattle,
Pacific Northwest, you know,

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.296
they did a lot of octaves,
like...

00:12:11.296 --> 00:12:17.702
Kind of like half time, like...

00:12:17.702 --> 00:12:18.804
♪ Yeah ♪

00:12:18.804 --> 00:12:22.341
[ Laughter ]

00:12:22.341 --> 00:12:24.242
♪ Yeah ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:12:24.242 --> 00:12:25.710
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:31.183
-Then like, Sleater-Kinney would
be, like, more single notes.

00:12:31.183 --> 00:12:33.952
♪ Don't go so slow ♪

00:12:33.952 --> 00:12:36.988
♪ Out of control ♪

00:12:36.988 --> 00:12:38.690
-Yeah, that's right. Love that.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:42.328
-And then like 2000,
things got very melodic,

00:12:42.328 --> 00:12:46.164
a lot of clear chords, you know.

00:12:46.164 --> 00:12:49.968
Like crooning, a lot of,
like, happy singing.

00:12:49.968 --> 00:12:51.670
You know, like...

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:55.040
♪ Come out with me again ♪

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.777
♪ I'd like to take you to
the stratosphere ♪

00:12:58.777 --> 00:12:59.912
Yeah, you know?

00:12:59.912 --> 00:13:03.415
[ Both singing indistinctly ]

00:13:03.415 --> 00:13:05.717
Kind of like Strokes kind of.
-Yeah, yeah, love that.

00:13:05.717 --> 00:13:07.119
[ Cheers and applause ]

